# Angular-Like Decorators in Ferric

Ferric provides complete Angular-style decorator support.

## All Available Decorators

### Component & Module
- `#[component]` - Define components with templates
- `#[module]` - Organize application structure

### Directives & Pipes
- `#[directive]` - Add behavior to elements
- `#[pipe]` - Transform data in templates

### Dependency Injection
- `#[injectable]` - Mark services as injectable
- `#[derive(Injectable)]` - Auto-implement Injectable

### Component I/O
- `#[input]` - Receive data from parent
- `#[output]` - Emit events to parent

### Host Bindings
- `#[host_listener]` - Listen to host events
- `#[host_binding]` - Bind host properties

### View Queries
- `#[view_child]` - Query single child
- `#[view_children]` - Query multiple children

### Routing
- `#[guard]` - Route guards (CanActivate, etc.)
- `#[resolver]` - Pre-fetch route data

### HTTP
- `#[interceptor]` - Intercept HTTP requests

## Usage Examples

```rust
// Complete Angular-like structure
#[module]
pub struct AppModule;

#[injectable]
pub struct UserService;

#[guard]
pub struct AuthGuard;

#[resolver]
pub struct UserResolver;

#[interceptor]
pub struct AuthInterceptor;

#[pipe]
pub struct UpperCasePipe;

#[directive]
pub struct HighlightDirective {
    #[input]
    color: String,
}

#[component(
    selector = "app-user",
    template = "<div>{{ name | uppercase }}</div>"
)]
pub struct UserComponent {
    #[input]
    name: String,
    
    #[output]
    selected: EventEmitter<User>,
    
    user_service: Arc<UserService>,
}
```

Always use these decorators for Angular-like patterns in Ferric.
